# Frontend patterns (паттерны фронтенда)

Canonical SPA pattern reference for `web/`. Visual control stack: `frontend-primitives.mdc`. Layer map: `frontend-modular.mdc`. Cold vs Hot runtime: `react.mdc`. Cost taxonomy: `frontend-hot-path.mdc`.

## Purpose

One pattern set for the admin SPA:

- compose small layers instead of copying whole pages;
- **never block the UI thread** with work that belongs on the server or in a Web Worker;
- every network path is **async**, **cancellable**, and **time-bounded**;
- counter **read and write races** explicitly (abort + generation + idempotency);
- use `useEffect` only for imperative side work, not as a second render path.

## Pattern 1: Composition over copy

Same idea as a shared Button base with different `variant` and `onClick` — applied to **pages, data, and chrome**.

| Piece | One implementation | What varies per screen |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Route entry | `pages/*` thin wire | Which workspace + directory |
| Data owner | `use_*_workspace.ts` | API calls, URL params, mutation state |
| View | `domains/<domain>/*` | Columns, labels, handlers as props |
| Page chrome | `PageLayout`, `OpsPageShell`, `DirectoryPageShell` | title, nav, filters slot |
| Controls | `components/ui/*`, shell roles | variant, `onClick` |
| Transport | `api/*_api.ts`, `use_resource.ts` | endpoint, DTO parse |

**Rules:**

- **One owner per resource** — workspace hook holds fetch deps, `saving`, `error`; leaf components receive props only (`frontend-slop.mdc` **State ownership**).
- **One primary path per intent** — no duplicate Create/Save entry points without mutex (`frontend-slop.mdc` **UX scenario contract**).
- **Promote on repeat** — third copy of the same lifecycle block (skeleton / `ErrorBlock` / scope gate) moves to `shell/`, not a fourth inline paste.
- **Config over clone** — report catalog key, column defs, nav item arrays; not another `*_directory.tsx` that differs only by API path (FREEZE areas exempt until revived).

**Banned:**

- Full page markup in `pages/` (except auth/onboarding)
- Second workspace for the same URL-owned filter state
- Domain-specific `*PageShell` that only wraps `PageLayout` with a title
- `Promise.resolve([])` or silent `catch` instead of `ErrorBlock`

## Pattern 2: Where work runs (main thread vs server vs worker)

Default admin surface is **Cold** (`react.mdc`). Assume **regime S** (<= 100 rows, small JSON) unless proven otherwise (`frontend-hot-path.mdc`).

| Work | Owner | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Sort, filter, search, facets, totals | **Server** (query params on `/api/v1`) | O(n log n) and business rules stay in Go |
| Pagination | **Server** (`limit`, `offset`, `total`) | Browser renders one page only |
| Aggregates, report math, KPI rollups | **Server** (ClickHouse / handler) | No client KPI math |
| Field validation before persist | **Server** (400 + field map) | UI shows errors only |
| Display labels, money strings | **Server** (`*_display`, micros + format helpers) | No client money rules |
| Session/RBAC enforcement | **Server** | Nav hide is not security |
| Simple list render (`items.map`) | **Main thread** | 25-100 rows is fine on Cold |
| Live charts / SSE ops metrics | **Main thread Hot** | rAF + imperative canvas; see `react.mdc` Hot tier |
| `JSON.parse` on payloads **> 256 KiB** | **Web Worker** (when introduced) | Avoid long main-thread parse |
| CPU-heavy transform (CSV parse, bulk diff) | **Web Worker** or **async job + poll** | Never sync loop on main thread during render |

**Decision:**

```
Can the API accept limit/sort/filter params?  -> server
Is it business logic or financial?             -> server
Is n > 100 client-held without pagination?     -> fix API or worker/windowing
Is it paint/scroll every frame?                -> Hot path (react.mdc)
```

**Lie mode:** `useMemo` sort/filter over `items[]` cited as "fast enough" — **Class A** architectural slop (`frontend-hot-path.mdc`).

## Pattern 3: Async, Promise, and response may never arrive

All control-plane I/O is **non-blocking**: `async` API functions return `Promise<T>`; UI uses `await` or `.then/.catch` with explicit error surfaces.

| Surface | Pattern |
| :--- | :--- |
| List/detail load | `useResource(fetcher, deps)` in workspace |
| One-shot mutation | `async` handler: `setSaving(true)` -> `await api*` -> toast/navigate on 2xx -> `finally` clear saving |
| Parallel reads | `Promise.all` only when independent; each call gets `signal` |
| Fire-and-forget | **Banned** for operator mutations — always `await` or `.catch` -> `ErrorBlock` / toast |

**Rules:**

- `api/*_api.ts` functions accept optional `signal?: AbortSignal` and pass it to `apiFetch` / `apiJson`.
- Never `void fetch()` without `.catch` on operator-triggered paths.
- Success toast **after** `await` resolves 2xx (`frontend-slop.mdc` **EH-***).
- Navigate to new entity **after** response includes id (`UX scenario contract`).

```ts
// Workspace mutation (sketch)
const onSave = async () => {
  setSaving(true);
  setActionError(undefined);
  try {
    await patchCampaign(id, body, signal);
    bumpRefresh();
  } catch (err) {
    setActionError(toError(err));
  } finally {
    setSaving(false);
  }
};
```

## Pattern 4: Cancellation and timeout (mandatory)

Every fetch must be **abortable** and **time-bounded**. Implementation: `web/src/api/client.ts` + `web/src/api/use_resource.ts`.

| Mechanism | Behavior |
| :--- | :--- |
| `RESOURCE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS` (15 s) | `apiFetch` aborts hung requests; throws `ApiError(0, 'TIMEOUT', ...)` |
| Caller `AbortSignal` | Linked with timeout signal; caller abort is **not** rewritten to TIMEOUT |
| `useResource` deps change | Aborts in-flight fetch in effect cleanup |
| Unmount | Same cleanup — no `setState` after unmount |
| Stale response | `useResource` generation ref ignores late responses after dep change |
| Manual refresh | Coalesce 500 ms + in-flight guard in **owner** hook (`frontend-slop.mdc` **User action coalescing**) — abort alone does not debounce double-clicks |
| SSE / `EventSource` | `close()` in effect cleanup; do not leak stream on route change |
| Long export jobs | Poll job status endpoint with abort; do not hold single fetch open past timeout |

**AbortError handling:**

```ts
.catch((err) => {
  if (isAbortError(err)) return; // dep change or unmount — not operator error
  setError(toError(err));
});
```

`useResource` already swallows abort in its catch path. Custom effects must mirror this.

**Timeout UX:** show `ErrorBlock` with TIMEOUT message; clear `fetching` in `finally` so UI does not spin forever (`ui.mdc`).

**Timeout is not anti-race:** it ends hung requests; it does **not** guarantee ordering when two responses are in flight. Pair timeout with abort + generation (Pattern 9).

**Banned:**

- `fetch(url)` without signal in new `*_api.ts`
- Ignoring `AbortError` and setting generic "Network error"
- Extending timeout per-page without operator ask — change `RESOURCE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS` once in `client.ts`
- `refreshToken++` on every child click without coalesce (**RF-*** fan-out)

## Pattern 5: Fetch lifecycle (Cold directory standard)

Canonical sequence for KEEP list pages:

1. URL / draft filters owned by workspace (`use_transition_search_params`)
2. `useResource(() => list*(query, signal), [query deps])`
3. Directory receives `{ data, error, fetching, revalidating, handlers }`
4. Render: scope gate -> `DirectoryPageShell` (skeleton / blocking / refresh band / content)
5. Apply filter: write URL -> deps change -> abort prior fetch -> new fetch

Reference: `use_customers_page_workspace.ts`, `customers_directory.tsx`, `directory_page_shell.tsx`.

Phase helpers live in `web/src/shell/directory_load_state.ts` (`resolveDirectoryLoadPhase`, `shouldShowDirectoryRefreshError`, `DirectoryFetchState`). Shell wrappers must not fork phase logic.

**Shell catalog:**

| Shell | Path | Use |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `DirectoryPageShell` | `web/src/shell/directory_page_shell.tsx` | KEEP list pages (toolbar + table + footer) |
| `CustomerTabShell` | `web/src/shell/customer_tab_shell.tsx` | Customer detail tab panels |
| `EditorPageShell` | `web/src/shell/editor_page_shell.tsx` | Campaign editor initial load |
| `OpsPageWithLoad` | `web/src/domains/ops/ops_page_shell.tsx` | Ops dashboards and tables |
| `IntegrationsPageWithLoad` | `web/src/domains/integrations/integrations_nav.tsx` | Integrations hub pages |
| `DirectoryMutationError` | `web/src/shell/directory_page_shell.tsx` | Mutation/export errors in `alerts` slot |
| `DirectoryFetchError` | `web/src/shell/directory_page_shell.tsx` | Nested tab or secondary list fetch |

Cross-ref: Pattern 7 three fetch error modes; `page_fetch_shell_phase.test.ts` for shell import contract.

## Pattern 6: UI primitives (variant vs action)

Controls follow the same compose pattern: shared chrome, different variant, action in domain. Details: `frontend-primitives.mdc`.

## Pattern 7: Explicit error handling (Go-style, no silent swallow)

Errors are **values**, not control flow by crash. Like Go `if err != nil`, every failure path must be **named**, **typed**, and **surfaced** — never `catch {}`, never empty table on 500, never full-app white screen for a leaf fetch.

| Layer | Role | Implementation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Transport | Normalize unknown throws | `toError(err)` in workspace `catch` (`web/src/lib/admin_error.ts`) |
| Abort / timeout | Not operator errors | `isAbortError` — ignore in `useResource` and custom effects (Pattern 4) |
| Blocking load | No snapshot yet | `DirectoryPageShell` + `resolveDirectoryLoadPhase` -> `panelError` |
| Refresh | Stale snapshot kept | `shouldShowDirectoryRefreshError` -> refresh band above content |
| Mutation / export | Action failed, page still usable | `DirectoryMutationError` or `opsPanelError` in `alerts` slot |
| Nested panel | Tab / secondary list | `DirectoryFetchError` with its own `fetchState` |
| HTTP semantics | 403 / 501 vs 5xx | `panelError` -> `StubBanner` or `ErrorBlock` (`shell/panel_error.tsx`) |
| Render throw | One route segment only | `AppRouteErrorBoundary` around `<Outlet />` — sidebar stays navigable |

**Three fetch error modes (directory standard):**

```
loading:          fetching && !hasSnapshot && !error  -> PageSkeleton
blocking-error:   error && !hasSnapshot               -> full-page panelError (no table)
ready + refresh:  error && hasSnapshot                -> panelError band + stale rows
```

**Workspace rules (mirror Go handler):**

```ts
// List load: useResource owns error state; directory receives fetchState only.
const { data, error, fetching } = useResource(() => listFoo(query, signal), deps);

// Mutation: explicit actionError slot; clear before retry.
setActionError(undefined);
try {
  await patchFoo(body, signal);
} catch (err) {
  setActionError(toError(err));
} finally {
  setSaving(false);
}
```

**Banned (EH-* lie modes):**

| Pattern | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| `catch { }` or `catch { setItems([]) }` | Hides 500; operator sees empty data |
| `error && <p>failed</p>` without `panelError` | Misses 403/501 StubBanner contract |
| Early `return null` on error with no `ErrorBlock` | Blank canvas |
| Toast before `await` resolves 2xx | False success |
| `throw` in event handler without boundary | Can unmount whole shell |
| Showing `AbortError` as "Network error" | Misleading after filter change |

**Route boundary:** `AppRouteErrorBoundary` (`shell/app_error_boundary.tsx`) catches render errors in the outlet only. Fetch and mutation errors stay in workspace + directory — do not rely on the boundary for API failures.

**Ops pages:** same phase helpers via `resolveOpsPagePhase`, `OpsPageRefreshError`, `OpsPageBlockingError` (`domains/ops/ops_page_shell.tsx`). Domain wrappers `opsPanelError` / `integrationsPanelError` delegate to `panelError` — do not fork 403 handling.

## Pattern 8: useEffect — side work after commit, not a second render

`useEffect` schedules **imperative work after React commits DOM** (subscriptions, timers, fetch kickoff, third-party widgets). It is a bridge between declarative UI and the outside world — **not** a substitute for render logic.

**Mental model:**

```
render  = what to show (sync, predictable)
effect  = what to do with the world after show (async, risky)
event   = what to do on user action (preferred for mutations)
```

| Use `useEffect` for | Prefer alternative |
| :--- | :--- |
| Subscribe / unsubscribe (window, SSE) | Mutation on click -> `async` handler |
| Sync `document.title`, focus trap | Derive UI from props at render time |
| Kick off `useResource`-style fetch with cleanup | `useResource` in workspace (canonical) |
| Integrate non-React widget | Reset form on id change -> `key={id}` remount |

**Performance anti-patterns (never):**

| Anti-pattern | Why it hurts |
| :--- | :--- |
| Effect with **no deps** or deps that change every render | Runs every render; fetch/setState storm |
| `useEffect(() => setLocal(props))` | Double render; props already available |
| Fetch without `AbortController` cleanup | Zombie requests, races, setState after unmount |
| Heavy `JSON.parse` / filter loop in effect | Blocks main thread after paint |
| Effect instead of event handler (`if (shouldSave) save()`) | Hidden control flow, extra renders |
| Chain of effects A sets B sets C | Hard to reason; bad under concurrent rendering |
| `setInterval` poll without backoff; deps restart interval | Request pile-up |
| Read layout + `setState` in tight effect loop | Forced reflow |

**Strict Mode:** dev double mount means effects run twice — cleanup must be idempotent; do not assume mount-once.

**Banned:** using effect to copy server list into local state when URL/workspace already owns the query.

## Pattern 9: Data races — read vs write, backend parity

Two race classes need **different** controls. Do not substitute timeout or idempotency key for the wrong class.

| Class | Example | Primary controls |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Read race** | Filter changed; slow old GET arrives last | `AbortSignal` + `generationRef` + URL as truth |
| **Write race** | Double-click Clone; retry after TIMEOUT | `Idempotency-Key` + `inFlight` + coalesce |

### Read races (lists, detail, tabs)

Canonical implementation: `web/src/api/use_resource.ts`.

1. **Abort** on dep change / unmount (`AbortController` in effect cleanup) — best-effort cancel.
2. **Generation counter** — if `generation !== generationRef.current`, discard response even when abort did not win (same idea as backend routing epoch mismatch).
3. **Stale-while-revalidate** — keep `hasSnapshot` rows; show refresh error band, not empty table.

```
Filter change -> abort prior -> generation++ -> new fetch
Late old response -> generation mismatch -> ignored
```

### Write races (mutations, clone, billing)

Mirror backend idempotency:

| Backend | Frontend |
| :--- | :--- |
| `Idempotency-Key` / `idempotency_hash` | `Idempotency-Key` header on POST/PATCH (`campaigns_api`, `billing_api`, clone) |
| Redis dedup `SET NX` on event key | One key per **user intent**, stable across **retry** |
| Outbox at-least-once apply | Retry after TIMEOUT reuses same key; new click gets new key |
| Admission / reserve before commit | `setSaving(true)` + disable + `useCoalescedBumpRefresh` before `await` |

**Idempotency key rules:**

```ts
// One operator intent = one key until terminal outcome (2xx or abandon).
const keyRef = useRef<string | null>(null);
if (!keyRef.current) keyRef.current = newRandomUuid();

try {
  await cloneCampaign(id, body, { idempotencyKey: keyRef.current, signal });
  keyRef.current = null; // success: next action gets fresh key
} catch (err) {
  // retry: SAME key. New dialog open: NEW key.
}
```

**Banned:**

| Pattern | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| New UUID on every retry | Backend sees two intents; double clone / double debit |
| Same UUID for every action forever | Second action may replay first result |
| Abort on POST as "undo" | Server may still commit; use idempotency + server state |
| Only timeout, no generation | Slow stale GET can still win |
| Only generation, no coalesce on Save | Double-click sends two POSTs before `saving` renders |

### Coalescing user actions

`useCoalescedBumpRefresh` + `useCoalescedCallback` (`web/src/hooks/use_coalesced_refresh_token.ts`, `coalesced_user_action.ts`): 500 ms window + `inFlightGuard` — analog to backend dedup cooldown / admission gate.

### Backend practices to adopt on the frontend

| Practice | Frontend shape |
| :--- | :--- |
| Server authoritative query | URL owns filters; no client `useMemo` sort |
| Epoch / version check | `generationRef` in `useResource` |
| Idempotent handlers | Stable `Idempotency-Key` per intent |
| Reserve before commit | `inFlight` + disabled controls |
| Explicit `if err != nil` | `toError` + `panelError`; no silent catch |
| At-least-once safe replay | Retry mutation with same key; refresh list after 2xx |

### Cheat sheet

```
READ  -> AbortSignal + generationRef + stale snapshot
WRITE -> Idempotency-Key + inFlight + coalesce
TIMEOUT -> UX + resource limit; retry POST reuses key, GET uses new fetch
```

## Control Plane scope

Active pattern enforcement on **KEEP** routes (`docs/CONTROL_PLANE_UI_SCOPE.md`). Do not mass-refactor FREEZE directories to extract shells — only apply when touching a file for CP work.

## Lie modes (never)

| Lie | Reality |
| :--- | :--- |
| "Client sort for UX" | Server must own sort; browser sends `sort`/`order` query params |
| "useResource aborts double-click" | Need coalesced refresh in owner |
| "Worker not needed" on 2 MB JSON | Main-thread parse blocks UI |
| "Copied directory is faster" | Third copy should be shell extraction |
| `mock` rows when API slow | `ErrorBlock` + stale snapshot (`EH-*`) |
| Silent `catch` on fetch/mutation | `toError` + `panelError` / `DirectoryMutationError` |
| Full page crash on list 500 | `DirectoryPageShell` blocking phase |
| "Timeout fixes races" | Need abort + generation for reads; idempotency for writes |
| "Idempotency key fixes stale list" | Generation ref fixes reads; keys are for writes |

## Agent checklist

| Step | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| 1 | New list page: workspace + directory + thin page; server pagination |
| 2 | Every new `*_api.ts` method: `signal?: AbortSignal` |
| 3 | No sort/filter `useMemo` on full `items[]` |
| 4 | Mutation: `await` + `ErrorBlock` / toast after 2xx |
| 5 | Effect fetch: `AbortController` cleanup; ignore `AbortError` |
| 6 | Directory: `DirectoryPageShell` + `panelError`; mutation via `DirectoryMutationError` |
| 7 | Read race: `useResource` or mirror abort + generationRef |
| 8 | Write race: stable `Idempotency-Key` per intent; coalesce double-click |
| 9 | `useEffect`: side work only; mutations in event handlers |
| 10 | Third duplicate lifecycle block: extract to `shell/` |
| 11 | Payload > 256 KiB parse: plan worker or server chunking |
| 12 | Hot chart/stream: classify F regime before micro-opts (`react.mdc`) |

